{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960681,"nonce":"FWSomFfMjHS0wUS1gAanBVU9qkE=","title":"an enum constructor in a switch pattern does not resolve through a wildcard import","message":"With the enum's module imported by wildcard, Rayzor cannot find its constructors in a `switch` over a value of that enum type. Haxe resolves them from the subject's type.\n\n    import window.*;   // window/Event.hx: enum Event { None; Resized(width:Int, height:Int); ... }\n\n    switch (w.poll()) {        // w.poll():Event\n        case Resized(width, height): ...\n    }\n\n    Error: [E0200] Cannot find name 'Resized'\n\n`import window.Event;` makes it compile. The same source compiles with Haxe 4.3.6 for HashLink and `--interp`.","files":null}]}